es.\" Christian subordination to authorities (Romans 13:1-7) is intended to enforce submission to leaders of the synagogues, not Roman government officials.","thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/561201-L.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"argument_driven","score":0.18,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"argument\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"Paul’s letter to the Romans reflects continuity with Judaism: its audience remains integral to Roman synagogue communities, with ‘weak’ non-Christian Jews, ‘strong’ Jewish and gentile believers, and ‘righteous gentiles’ guided by Jewish rules.","confidence":0.61},"academicOrientation":{"score":62,"confidence":0.4},"profileConfidence":0.52,"lowerConfidenceCandidates":{"centralPlaces":[{"name":"Roman","confidence":0.4}]},"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion":8,"inputHash":"fa669e3f553159f5db51c0ec23b6d982fd6153f8884b9218eda9566e85a7c57e","reviewStatus":"unreviewed","validationWarnings":[]},"displaySummary":"The \"weak\" are non- Christian Jews, while the \"strong\" included both Jewish and gentile converts to belief in Jesus. Paul as a practicing devout Jew insists on the rules of behavior for \"the righteous gentiles.\" Christian subordination to authorities (Romans 13:1-7) is intended to enforce submission to leaders of the synagogues, not Roman government officials.","primarySubject":"Religion","primaryTopic":"Religion & Religious Movements","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Religion","confidence":"low","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Religion","score":6,"evidenceCount":3},{"subject":"Politics & Government","score":3,"evidenceCount":2}],"evidence":[{"source":"keyword_classifier","rawLabel":"Politics & Government","mappedSubject":"Politics